<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<inkscape-extension xmlns="http://www.inkscape.org/namespace/inkscape/extension">
<name>NextDraw Plot Digest (Plob) Export</name>
<id>command.bantamtools.nextdraw-plob</id>
<dependency type="extension">org.inkscape.output.svg.inkscape</dependency>
<dependency type="executable" location="extensions">nextdraw_control.py</dependency>
<image>nextdraw_deps/nextdrawcore/inx_img/nextdraw_plob_header.svg</image>

<param name="digest" type="int" gui-hidden="true">2</param>

<param name="submode" type="notebook">
<page name="Plot Digest Settings" gui-text="Plot Digest Options">

<hbox >
<image width="50" height="10">nextdraw_deps/nextdrawcore/inx_img/spacer_10px.svg</image>
<vbox >
<param name="model" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo" indent="1" gui-text="Model:">
<option value="0">- Select -</option>
<option value="8">Bantam Tools NextDraw™ 8511</option>
<option value="9">Bantam Tools NextDraw™ 1117</option>
<option value="10">Bantam Tools NextDraw™ 2234</option>
<option value="1">AxiDraw V2, V3, or SE/A4</option>
<option value="2">AxiDraw V3/A3 or SE/A3</option>
<option value="6">AxiDraw SE/A2</option>
<option value="5">AxiDraw SE/A1</option>
<option value="7">AxiDraw V3/B6</option>
<option value="4">AxiDraw MiniKit</option>
<option value="3">AxiDraw V3 XLX</option>
</param>


<param indent="1" name="mode" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo" gui-text="Layer handling:">
<option value="plot">Include all layers</option>
<option value="layers">Only specific layer(s)...</option>
</param>
<param indent="5" name="layer" type="int" min="0" max="1000"
gui-text="Specific layer selection:">1</param>

<spacer />

<param indent="1" name="reordering" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo" gui-text="Plot optimization:">
<option value="0">Least; Only connect adjoining paths</option>
<option value="1">Basic; Also reorder paths for speed</option>
<option value="2">Full; Also allow path reversal</option>
<option value="4">None; Strictly preserve file order</option>
</param>

<param indent="3" name="auto_rotate" type="bool" gui-text="Auto-rotate page when printing"
gui-description="Pages taller than wide will be rotated 90 degrees counter-clockwise when printed."
>true</param>	
<param indent="3" name="random_start" type="bool" gui-text="Randomize starts of closed paths">false</param>
<param indent="3" name="hiding" type="bool" gui-text="Hidden-line removal"
gui-description="Tip: Hidden-line removal can be slow. It also ignores path orientation, so full optimization is recommended."
>false</param>


</vbox>
</hbox>

<image width="10" height="5">nextdraw_deps/nextdrawcore/inx_img/spacer_10px.svg</image>
<image>nextdraw_deps/nextdrawcore/inx_img/nd_hr.svg</image>
<image width="10" height="5">nextdraw_deps/nextdrawcore/inx_img/spacer_10px.svg</image>

<label indent="6">Version 1.7.5      —      Copyright 2026 Bantam Tools</label>

</page>

<page name="help" gui-text="About">
<label indent="1">
The Plot Digest Object or "Plob" format is a limited subset of SVG,
stripped of style information and prepared plotting.
</label>
<label indent="1">
Generating the Plob is destructive. Always save as a separate
copy and keep your original, editable document intact.
</label>
<spacer />
<label indent="1">
The NextDraw software pre-processes documents into Plob format as part
of the printing process. This process strips out layers and objects
that won't be printed as well as all styles. It reduces the document
to a simplified plot-ready format, clipping to the plot area, and
applying any optimizations.
</label>
<label indent="1">
A Plob document prepared for a specific model of supported plotter,
if not further edited, can be printed on that same plotter model,
by the same Bantam Tools NextDraw software version, without further
processing. This can potentially save a large amount of time when
repeatedly starting or resuming a plot.
</label>

<spacer />

<label indent="1">
Exporting a Plob may be helpful in certain situations, for example when
working with extremely large files, in order to
separate the processing and motion-control stages of plotting.
</label>
</page>

</param>

<output>
        <extension>.svg</extension>
        <mimetype>image/svg+xml</mimetype>
        <filetypename>NextDraw "Plob" Plot Digest (*.svg)</filetypename>
        <filetypetooltip>Plob file for NextDraw</filetypetooltip>
        <savecopyonly>true</savecopyonly>
</output>

<script>
<command location="extensions" interpreter="python">nextdraw_control.py</command>
</script>

</inkscape-extension>

